  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Request and cache flow",
      "items": [
        "Browser asks CloudFront over HTTPS; plain HTTP gets a 301 redirect to HTTPS. Only GET and HEAD are allowed; responses are compressed.",
        "Fresh cached objects are served at the edge. A miss or stale object triggers a SigV4-signed request (OAC) to the private S3 REST endpoint.",
        "The cache policy uses TTL min/default 0 and max 1 year, so S3 Cache-Control headers decide: no-cache for HTML and payloads, one-year immutable for fingerprinted _nuxt assets.",
        "The AWS managed security-headers policy adds HSTS, X-Content-Type-Options, X-Frame-Options, Referrer-Policy and X-XSS-Protection to every response.",
        "Only / maps to index.html. There is no SPA fallback: a key that does not exist returns 403 from S3 through CloudFront; nested URLs need a CloudFront rewrite."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "All nine Terraform resources",
      "items": [
        "1. CloudFront distribution: redirect-to-https, GET/HEAD, compression, default certificate, index.html root object.",
        "2. Origin Access Control: always signs origin requests with SigV4.",
        "3. Cache policy: TTL 0/0/31536000; gzip and Brotli; no cookies, headers or query strings in the cache key. (Security headers policy is AWS-managed, read as a data source.)",
        "4. S3 bucket in ap-southeast-1; website hosting disabled.",
        "5. Public-access block: all four blocks on.",
        "6. Ownership controls: BucketOwnerEnforced disables ACLs.",
        "7. Encryption: SSE-S3 (AES256) by default.",
        "8. Lifecycle rule: abort incomplete multipart uploads after 7 days.",
        "9. Bucket policy (dev root): CloudFront s3:GetObject only when AWS:SourceArn is this distribution; deny any request without TLS."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Build, publish, provision",
      "items": [
        "Terraform provisions infrastructure only; it never uploads site files. State is local by default, or in the lesson 10-11 S3 bucket if you opt in.",
        "pnpm generate writes nuxt-app/.output/public. The AWS CLI uploads fingerprinted _nuxt assets first, stable files second, HTML last, then invalidates /* and waits.",
        "Uploads are not atomic; avoid concurrent releases. The dev example sets force_destroy = true, so destroy deletes all objects.",
        "Configured from source on 2026-10-22; the stack is currently destroyed. This is not a live AWS inventory."
      ]
    }
  ]
